      textEn: 'Emotion which is suffering ceases to be suffering as soon as we form a clear and precise picture of it. The act of understanding an emotion transforms it from a wild storm that tosses you about to a weather pattern that you can observe, predict, and navigate. Anger examined becomes something different from anger blindly expressed; grief understood becomes something different from grief blindly endured. The rational person does not suppress emotions but illuminates them, bringing the light of awareness into the dark chambers of the psyche until every shadow has a name and every demon has a story. This is not cold detachment but the warmest form of self-compassion.',
